{"path":"s73","heading":"Settlement agreement.","in_1996":true,"nodes_1996":[{"path":"s73","node_type":"section","number":"73","heading":"Settlement agreement.","text":""},{"path":"s73.ss1","node_type":"subsection","number":"1","heading":null,"text":"When it appears to the conciliator that there exist elements of a settlement which may be acceptable to the parties, he shall formulate the terms of a possible settlement and submit them to the parties for their observations. After receiving the observations of the parties, the conciliator may reformulate the terms of a possible settlement in the light of such observations."},{"path":"s73.ss2","node_type":"subsection","number":"2","heading":null,"text":"If the parties reach agreement on a settlement of the dispute, they may draw up and sign a written settlement agreement. If requested by the parties, the conciliator may draw up, or assist the parties in drawing up, the settlement agreement."},{"path":"s73.ss3","node_type":"subsection","number":"3","heading":null,"text":"When the parties sign the settlement agreement, it shall be final and binding on the parties and persons claiming under them respectively."},{"path":"s73.ss4","node_type":"subsection","number":"4","heading":null,"text":"The conciliator shall authenticate the settlement agreement and furnish a copy thereof to each of the parties."}],"events":[]}